          <Pad Id="xg5uHAAqnEoUffMhl0v6Lb" Comment="Title" Bounds="182,1076,190,19" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="HowTo Build a Path">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl"><Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" /></p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="iJhdd8yhm32IUzij3ATGmz" Bounds="85,1170,830,340" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Drag the points in the Renderer. Each point is a Point node (a Circle with Drag, defined in this patch) and its Position output goes to the path node. Columns 1 and 2 use one ForEach region over a Spread of start positions (Translation), GetSlice hands every position to its node. The Point elements come after the paths in the Group, so they stay visible and draggable.&#xD;&#xA;- LineTo (Relative) takes an offset from the last point, a Point gives an absolute position: Subtract computes Position minus the previous point. Column 3 (AddRoundRect) is fixed.&#xD;&#xA;- Points are in units of the Renderer Space (1 unit = 100 DIP, origin top left), angles in cycles (1 = full turn), like Skia. A path never changes: a node returns a new path when one of its inputs changes, so one path can feed several Path nodes.&#xD;&#xA;- ArcTo (tangent) rounds the corner between the last point, Corner and Destination Point. ArcTo (SVG) is the SVG arc command: Radius, X Axis Rotate, Large Arc, Sweep, Destination Point. The oval form takes Bounds, Start Angle, Sweep Angle and Force Move To.&#xD;&#xA;- Add... nodes start a new contour. An unconnected Input starts a new path, so AddRoundRect alone is enough in column 3. Close joins the end of a contour with its start.&#xD;&#xA;- A path must fit one command to Qt (about 65 000 bytes): roughly 7270 line segments, a curve takes more room than a line. A bigger path is not drawn and the Path node warns with the counts.&#xD;&#xA;- Skia: the nodes of Graphics.Skia.Paths (MoveTo, LineTo, CubicTo, ArcTo, Close, AddRect, AddRoundRect ...) and the Path layer. Fill and Stroke are one Path node here.&#xD;&#xA;- Connect it to Renderer [Qt] or a Group [Qt].">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl"><Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" /></p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="ogwVzeBgnm4JnZk5O3pJQl" Bounds="85,268,326,29" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Drag the points in the Renderer">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
